# Production deployment env (ADR 0007). Copy to `.env` on the server and fill in
# real values. `docker-compose.prod.yml` reads it via `env_file` — never commit
# the filled-in `.env` (only this example is tracked).
#
# For LOCAL DEVELOPMENT you do NOT use this file. Dev only containerizes
# Postgres; the API reads apps/api/.env instead. See apps/api/.env.example.

# --- Postgres container (docker-compose.prod.yml `insuredesk-db-prod`) ------
POSTGRES_USER="insuredesk"
POSTGRES_PASSWORD="change-me-to-a-strong-password"
POSTGRES_DB="insuredesk"

# --- Release image (docker-compose.prod.yml `insuredesk-api-prod`, ADR 0009) -
# The release tag to run, pinned here so the server always knows which version
# it is on. Upgrade = change this to the new tag, then `pull insuredesk-api-prod`
# + `up -d`
# (see docs/releasing.md). GHCR is private: `docker login ghcr.io` with a PAT
# (read:packages) before pulling.
IMAGE_TAG="v2026.07.0"

# --- API runtime (docker-compose.prod.yml `insuredesk-api-prod`) ------------
# DATABASE_URL host is the compose SERVICE NAME `insuredesk-db-prod` (not
# localhost): the API container reaches Postgres over the compose network.
# User/password/db must match the POSTGRES_* values above.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://insuredesk:change-me-to-a-strong-password@insuredesk-db-prod:5432/insuredesk?schema=public"

# Must be "production" — enables SPA static serving and secure cookies.
NODE_ENV="production"

# Session secret for signing cookies. Generate a long random string, e.g.:
#   openssl rand -hex 32
SESSION_SECRET="change-me-use-a-long-random-string-min-32-chars"

# Optional overrides (sensible defaults baked into the image):
# HOST defaults to 0.0.0.0 (inside the container); compose binds it to
# 127.0.0.1:3000 on the host, so the API is never directly public.
# PORT defaults to 3000. LOG_LEVEL defaults to info.
# SESSION_MAX_AGE_SECONDS defaults to 86400 (24h).
# WEB_DIST_PATH defaults to /app/apps/web/dist in the image — leave unset.
# LOG_LEVEL="info"
# SESSION_MAX_AGE_SECONDS="86400"

# --- Backup sidecar (docker-compose.prod.yml `backup`, ADR 0009) ------------
# Host directory the daily backups land in (bind-mounted into the sidecar).
# Defaults to $HOME/backups/insuredesk — uncomment to relocate, using an
# absolute path (a bare ~ is not reliably expanded in a compose bind mount).
# BACKUP_DIR="/srv/backups/insuredesk"

# --- Build-time mirrors (restricted networks, e.g. mainland China) ----------
# Only used by the local-build fallback (`docker compose ... up -d --build`
# when GHCR is unreachable). Default to official sources. Uncomment on a
# network where npmjs.org / binaries.prisma.sh are unreachable.
# NPM_REGISTRY="https://registry.npmmirror.com"
# PRISMA_ENGINES_MIRROR="https://registry.npmmirror.com/-/binary/prisma"
